WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:01.833
- What's the biggest thing
I should maybe be concerned

00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:04.125
about as an American citizen?

00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:05.582
- Going back to Trump's twitter,

00:00:05.582 --> 00:00:08.726
(horn sounding)

00:00:08.726 --> 00:00:11.649
he tweeted on February
17, 'The fake news media,

00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:15.709
failing New York Times,
NBC News, ABC, CBS, CNN,

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:18.963
is not my enemy, it is the
enemy of the American people.'

00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:20.328
- Is he not an American person?

00:00:20.328 --> 00:00:22.296
- I mean this is concerning because

00:00:22.296 --> 00:00:24.129
it kinda seems like
it's maybe contradicting

00:00:24.129 --> 00:00:26.072
the first Amendment of the Constitution.

00:00:26.072 --> 00:00:27.088
A little bit.

00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:28.235
- That's the first one.

00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:29.185
- It's the number one.

00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:30.820
- It's the best Amendment.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.688
- It's the number one top Amendment.

00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:34.327
So but basically that one is protecting

00:00:34.327 --> 00:00:36.534
like freedom of speech, freedom of press,

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.518
you know, and he's not taking away any

00:00:38.518 --> 00:00:40.007
of their freedoms, but he's kind of like

00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:42.390
placing this distrust and sort of

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.345
discrediting them a little bit.

00:00:44.345 --> 00:00:45.681
- Here's my biggest concern right now,

00:00:45.681 --> 00:00:47.145
and this might be selfish.

00:00:47.145 --> 00:00:50.067
I'm a media person, and he
certainly didn't call out

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.923
BuzzFeed in this instance, as before.

00:00:52.923 --> 00:00:56.088
Is Trump potentially
telling the American people

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:57.722
that I'm their enemy?

00:00:57.722 --> 00:00:58.616
- I don't know.

00:00:58.616 --> 00:01:00.638
- Because if I'm their
enemy, I want more stuff.

00:01:00.638 --> 00:01:03.349
I want a lair, I want a badass car.

00:01:03.349 --> 00:01:06.912
I want space weapons, I want
expensive wine all the time

00:01:06.912 --> 00:01:08.798
that I could be like
constantly doing this.

00:01:08.798 --> 00:01:10.819
I want better stuff if
I'm going to be an enemy.

00:01:10.819 --> 00:01:12.312
Enemies have cool stuff.

00:01:12.312 --> 00:01:13.145
- It's true.

00:01:13.145 --> 00:01:13.984
- Can we call Hayes?

00:01:13.984 --> 00:01:15.511
- I think we should
check back in with Hayes,

00:01:15.511 --> 00:01:17.528
and see what he thinks.

00:01:17.528 --> 00:01:19.067
- Hey guys, I missed you.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.332
- Hey.

00:01:20.332 --> 00:01:22.214
- We're talking about
the tweet that Trump sent

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:24.725
saying that all the news
outlets were an enemy

00:01:24.725 --> 00:01:26.174
of the American people.

00:01:26.174 --> 00:01:28.607
I want to know, since I
technically work for a media

00:01:28.607 --> 00:01:30.553
company that has a news outlet,

00:01:30.553 --> 00:01:34.180
a, if I am then an enemy to the people,

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.986
and b, if you are an even
bigger enemy to the people,

00:01:37.986 --> 00:01:40.236
and c, what does this mean?

00:01:41.886 --> 00:01:43.533
- Well, first of all,
as far as I can tell,

00:01:43.533 --> 00:01:45.609
being an enemy of the state
is a transitive property

00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:47.677
so it's like a six degrees
of separation thing.

00:01:47.677 --> 00:01:50.765
If you know someone who's an
enemy of the American people

00:01:50.765 --> 00:01:53.041
and are like relatively
close ties with them,

00:01:53.041 --> 00:01:55.474
it passes on to you like a cold.

00:01:55.474 --> 00:01:57.062
- Oh.

00:01:57.062 --> 00:01:58.113
- That's just my working theory.

00:01:58.113 --> 00:01:59.296
- So you are a bigger enemy than me,

00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:00.370
but I am still an enemy.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:02.147
- Yes, correct, because you work

00:02:02.147 --> 00:02:03.957
for this failing pile of garbage as well.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.440
- I aspire to your position sir.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.824
- In all seriousness, it's
really terrible and scary.

00:02:09.824 --> 00:02:10.980
- Yeah.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.669
- So today in CPAC, Trump
had a speech where he tried

00:02:13.669 --> 00:02:15.639
to say no, no, no, I
was just talking about

00:02:15.639 --> 00:02:18.169
the fake news and journalists
who make up sources,

00:02:18.169 --> 00:02:20.922
which happens to be everyone in my mind.

00:02:20.922 --> 00:02:22.917
The fact that he's
trying to say that anyone

00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:26.136
who disagrees with him is
automatically a liar and fake,

00:02:26.136 --> 00:02:30.863
is a way to sort of burrow away
at the idea of a free press

00:02:30.863 --> 00:02:35.333
in a way which you would
expect to see in a less free

00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:37.205
country than the United States of America.

00:02:37.205 --> 00:02:39.658
Trump today again at CPAC said
something along the lines of

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:41.489
I don't mind bad stories
when I've earned them,

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:43.371
except he seems to never believe

00:02:43.371 --> 00:02:45.010
that he's truly earned them.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.262
And it goes back to our
good friend, Vladimir Putin,

00:02:47.262 --> 00:02:51.309
in similarities when you
see how the Russian state

00:02:51.309 --> 00:02:53.381
controls most of the media.

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:55.541
And you have very few
independent outlets left.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.293
- Who else in history,
you can name all of them,

00:02:58.293 --> 00:03:02.485
has made an enemy of the press
to the people they represent?

00:03:02.485 --> 00:03:06.292
- Oh, you know, some dudes
named Benito, Adolph,

00:03:06.292 --> 00:03:09.861
Uncle Joe, just some friendly characters,

00:03:09.861 --> 00:03:11.951
Bobby Mugabe down in Zimbabwe.

00:03:11.951 --> 00:03:14.036
- As a person who technically
according to Trump

00:03:14.036 --> 00:03:16.980
is an enemy, would you
ever go on record saying

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.070
something like Trump
is kind of like Hitler?

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.073
- Mmm, no, bit soon, bit soon for that.

00:03:23.073 --> 00:03:23.937
- Yeah.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:26.051
- Okay, I said...

00:03:26.051 --> 00:03:28.264
- So basically what he would
say, this is a potential

00:03:28.264 --> 00:03:30.607
first step in the wrong direction.

00:03:30.607 --> 00:03:32.641
- Wrong direction, will agree with that.

00:03:32.641 --> 00:03:35.209
I've been reading a
lovely Hitler biography,

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:38.888
and there are some things
where I'm like, I see.

00:03:38.888 --> 00:03:41.971
I see, but we're not quite there yet.

00:03:42.905 --> 00:03:44.460
- Well I appreciate your time,

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.613
and since I aspire to be a bigger villain,

00:03:46.613 --> 00:03:48.497
I'm not really a reporter,
so I do think Trump

00:03:48.497 --> 00:03:50.069
is probably very Hitler-like,

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:51.600
but you don't have to say that,

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.157
and I'm not technically news so...

00:03:53.157 --> 00:03:55.688
- Bye, signing off, bye.

00:03:55.688 --> 00:03:58.423
- Like I don't know if
Trump is actually Hitler,

00:03:58.423 --> 00:04:00.950
I don't know if Trump is actually Putin.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:04.238
You know, he's going to be
his own kind of person, right.

00:04:04.238 --> 00:04:06.159
No one can be Hitler, Hitler is Hitler.

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:08.771
No one can be Keith Habersberger,
I'm Keith Habersberger.

00:04:08.771 --> 00:04:11.057
That's just the facts, right.

00:04:11.057 --> 00:04:13.511
- Those are both facts,
you are not Hitler,

00:04:13.511 --> 00:04:15.273
Trump is not Hitler.

00:04:15.273 --> 00:04:16.271
- Trump is not Keith.

00:04:16.271 --> 00:04:17.288
- Trump is not Keith.

00:04:17.288 --> 00:04:18.660
You are not Trump.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.569
These are true things.

00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:22.741
- I'm making everybody who's
like an authority of facts,

00:04:22.741 --> 00:04:24.186
very worried right now.

00:04:24.186 --> 00:04:25.835
- Those of us who like facts and truth

00:04:25.835 --> 00:04:27.201
were really concerned.

00:04:27.201 --> 00:04:29.542
We don't want to make
too many crazy claims.

00:04:29.542 --> 00:04:31.623
We're really nervous right now.

00:04:31.623 --> 00:04:34.670
- It's scary to make crazy
claims, but right now

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.978
Trump has made it scary
to make factual claims.

00:04:37.978 --> 00:04:40.046
- Or it seems like he's
trying to make people

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:43.437
not believe like accurate reporting.

00:04:43.437 --> 00:04:45.645
- He's turning us against ourselves.

00:04:45.645 --> 00:04:48.173
It's kinda like, kinda like...

00:04:48.173 --> 00:04:49.200
- [Man] Hunger Games?

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.944
- Hunger Games, yeah,
kinda like Hunger Games.

00:04:51.944 --> 00:04:53.285
I was going to go for Hitler, but actually

00:04:53.285 --> 00:04:54.451
it's way more like Hunger Games.

00:04:54.451 --> 00:04:57.049
- No, it's pretty Hunger Gamesy.

00:04:57.049 --> 00:04:58.390
I'm safe with Hunger Games.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.091
- Nah, it's fiction.

00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:01.326
Why can't I just say that he's Hitler?

00:05:01.326 --> 00:05:02.425
Why can't I just say it?

00:05:02.425 --> 00:05:03.731
Like I just want to know why

00:05:03.731 --> 00:05:04.564
I can't just make crazy claims?

00:05:04.564 --> 00:05:06.328
- It's too much right now.

00:05:06.328 --> 00:05:07.707
- Well I'm an enemy, no one's
going to believe me anyway.

